    <briefdescription>
<para>Partitioning algorithm. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a recursive search algorithm that can explore multiple possiblities.</para>
<para>When a cluster of nodes can go into more than one partition, and we haven&apos;t reached maximum search depth, we recurse and explore both options and their consequences. Both branches will yield a proposal, and the driver will grade both and choose the best one.</para>
<para>If max depth is reached, we will use some heuristics to make a choice. Most of the time we will just use the least-pressured (cheapest) partition, but if a cluster is particularly big and there is a good amount of overlap with an existing partition, we will choose that partition instead. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
